  "goodToKnow": "Die Leiharbeit (also Zeitarbeit) is temporary agency work: an agency employs workers and lends them to other companies. Under the Arbeitnehmerüberlassungsgesetz, agency workers may usually be placed in the same company for at most 18 months and should receive equal pay after nine months. Der Leiharbeiter is an agency worker. Leihen means to lend or borrow. It has no plural."
